    "heading": "Interacting with Objects",
    "lineStart": 1317,
    "lineEnd": 1321
  },
  "section": "1.48",
  "rulesText": "Interacting with objects is often simple to resolve. The player tells the GM that their character is doing something, such as moving a lever or opening\n\na door, and the GM describes what happens. Sometimes, however, rules govern what you can do with an object, as detailed in the following sections."
}
